PS5: a test switch to scan a frame out of system memory when VRAM has no room for it

amdgpu pins every frame it shows as one contiguous block of VRAM, unless the buffer was created write-combined, which
a game's swapchain is not. On a PS5 the VRAM is a fixed carve-out (vram.txt): a game that fills it leaves no room for
the next frame, the pin fails ("Failed to pin framebuffer: -ENOMEM"), gamescope aborts and the session falls back to
the desktop. Seen with Predecessor and Expedition 33, most often with 4 GB of VRAM (issues #63 and #64).

The display can read a frame from system memory with S/G display, which amdgpu leaves off on the PS5's display IP
(2.0.3) unless amdgpu.sg_display=1 is given at boot. With that and amdgpu.ps5_scanout_gtt=1 (the latter also at runtime
in /sys/module/amdgpu/parameters), a pin that fails with -ENOMEM is retried in GTT; amdgpu_bo_pin() narrows a VRAM|GTT
request to the buffer's preferred VRAM, so the retry asks for GTT alone. Only for CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH, never for the
cursor. Otherwise the first such failure logs once what is missing.

Off by default: amdgpu_display_supported_domains() allows GTT scanout only for write-combined buffers because other
placements hung the display on some APUs, and whether the PS5 is one of them is not known. Compiled; not run on a PS5.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
index a2b8f7033..3311c76c0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
@@ -1199,6 +1199,17 @@ int amdgpu_dm_plane_fill_plane_buffer_attributes(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
 }
 EXPORT_IF_KUNIT(amdgpu_dm_plane_fill_plane_buffer_attributes);
 
+/*
+ * PS5: amdgpu pins a frame as one contiguous block of VRAM, and a game that fills the VRAM carve-out leaves
+ * none, which ends the compositor. With this set, such a frame is scanned out of system memory instead. That
+ * needs S/G display, which amdgpu leaves off on this display IP (2.0.3) unless amdgpu.sg_display=1 is given
+ * at boot. Off by default: amdgpu only allows GTT scanout for write-combined buffers, because others have
+ * hung the display on some APUs, and a game's swapchain is not write-combined. Can be switched at runtime.
+ */
+static bool ps5_scanout_gtt;
+module_param(ps5_scanout_gtt, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ps5_scanout_gtt, "PS5: scan a frame out of system memory when VRAM has no room for it; needs amdgpu.sg_display=1 (test, default off)");
+
 static int amdgpu_dm_plane_helper_prepare_fb(struct drm_plane *plane,
 					     struct drm_plane_state *new_state)
 {
@@ -1243,6 +1254,21 @@ static int amdgpu_dm_plane_helper_prepare_fb(struct drm_plane *plane,
 
 	rbo->flags |= AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_VRAM_CONTIGUOUS;
 	r = amdgpu_bo_pin(rbo, domain);
+	/* amdgpu_bo_pin() narrows a VRAM|GTT request to the buffer's preferred VRAM: ask for GTT alone */
+	if (r == -ENOMEM && READ_ONCE(ps5_scanout_gtt) && plane->type != DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR &&
+	    adev->asic_type == CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH && adev->mode_info.gpu_vm_support) {
+		r = amdgpu_bo_pin(rbo, AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_GTT);
+		if (!r)
+			drm_info_once(adev_to_drm(adev),
+				      "no room in VRAM for a frame, scanning out of system memory\n");
+	} else if (r == -ENOMEM && adev->asic_type == CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH && plane->type != DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR) {
+		if (!adev->mode_info.gpu_vm_support)
+			drm_info_once(adev_to_drm(adev),
+				      "no room in VRAM for a frame; system memory needs amdgpu.sg_display=1 and amdgpu.ps5_scanout_gtt=1 (test)\n");
+		else
+			drm_info_once(adev_to_drm(adev),
+				      "no room in VRAM for a frame; amdgpu.ps5_scanout_gtt=1 tries system memory (test)\n");
+	}
 	if (unlikely(r != 0)) {
 		if (r != -ERESTARTSYS)
 			DRM_ERROR("Failed to pin framebuffer: %pe\n", ERR_PTR(r));
